ios: tap to drop

For the mobile HUD's drop button (as on OSRS mobile): setTapToDrop(on) makes a tap on an item in the inventory tab
drop it (the item's fifth op, OP_HELD5: "Drop", or what the item calls it) instead of doing its first op. The tap is
the item drag's release (mouseLoop's objDragArea): where upstream does the top menu entry, tapDropOption picks the
drop entry of the same slot and component. Only when the top entry is one of the item's own ops in the tab panel, so
a long-press (the menu), a drag (moving the item), a use or target mode ("Use Tinderbox with...", a spell on an item)
and the inventories of side modals (bank, shop, trade, whose items have other ops) are unchanged. hudState() reports
tapToDrop. Off (the default), nothing changes.

